        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Blessed is a likeable pea protein with real strengths: 23 g of single-source pea protein per scoop, stevia instead of sucralose, a useful dose of iron and a flavor range buyers mostly enjoy. Its weaknesses are just as clear. It has no NSF or Informed Sport certification we could find, newer flavors carry 600 mg or more of sodium, and at about $1.99 per 25 g it costs two to three times as much as a plain pea isolate.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If you are vegan, not drug tested and want a flavored shake straight from the tub, Blessed is a fair buy, best on the two-bag Strawberry Mylk deal or during an EHPlabs sale. If you want certification, buy NOW Sports Pea Protein; if you want value, buy Naked Pea; and if you want a flavored shake with Prime shipping, OWYN Pro Elite is the swap. Our <a href="/best-plant-based-protein-powder/">plant-based protein rankings</a> cover the rest of the field.
